    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0763" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg751"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.00/612: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-28T18:00:00-04:00">January 28, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. From the Under Secretary for Lieutenant Colonel Hoskins. Your 153, January
                    23, 9 a.m., has been read with interest and you may be sure that we are giving
                    it careful thought. Our present feeling is that it would be inadvisable to bring
                    groups of Arabs and Jews to this country for a discussion of the Palestine
                    problem. However, the suggestion has been made that Ibn Saud<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d800-f1"/> be asked to designate one of his sons to come here for a
                        visit.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d800-f2"/> The invitation would, of course, be
                    extended to the King in the first instance but since it is assumed that he would
                    find it impracticable to accept, it would be made clear that we would be glad to
                    have one of his three eldest sons visit this country, should the King himself
                    find it impossible to come. It is felt that such a visit would accomplish at
                    least some of the purposes you have in mind. Please discuss this suggestion with
                    the Minister and let us have your views. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d800-f1" n="11" xml:id="d800-f1-content">
                <p>Abdul Aziz ibn Saud, King of Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d800-f2" n="12" xml:id="d800-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the visit of Amir Faisal to the United States, see
                        <ref target="#pg840">pp. 840</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
